From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: /sdapi/v1/txt2img and img2img find a LoRA added
 since the last listing

The A1111 routes looked a "lora" path up in the cache that only
GET /sdapi/v1/loras and the sdcpp routes refresh, so a LoRA uploaded or
downloaded after the start failed with "invalid lora path" until a client
listed the LoRAs. They refresh it now, as the sdcpp routes do.

---
 examples/server/routes_sdapi.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/examples/server/routes_sdapi.cpp b/examples/server/routes_sdapi.cpp
--- a/examples/server/routes_sdapi.cpp
+++ b/examples/server/routes_sdapi.cpp
@@ -153,6 +153,7 @@
     }

     if (j.contains("lora") && j["lora"].is_array()) {
+        refresh_lora_cache(runtime);  // PS5SD: a LoRA added since the last listing
         request.gen_params.lora_map.clear();
         request.gen_params.high_noise_lora_map.clear();

